# What is deliberately NOT published, and why.
#
# The repository ships everything needed to reproduce the paper's results and to
# use the model. It does not ship bulk inputs that are either (a) redistributions
# of someone else's archive, or (b) regenerable from a script in this repo. Each
# exclusion below names the script that recreates it.

# --- Raw third-party archives (4.2 GB). Redistributing them would fork a
# --- maintained dataset. Fetch with scripts/prepare_data.py, which downloads
# --- the NIST ThermoML archive (doi:10.18434/mds2-2422) directly.
data/raw/

# --- Synthetic training pool (1.1 GB, 21.7M states). Fully regenerable and
# --- seed-pinned: scripts/generate_synthetic.py then scripts/relabel_detail.py.
# --- data/synthetic/MANIFEST.md IS tracked so the sampling rules are public.
data/synthetic/*.parquet

# --- Redundant CSV mirror of a tracked parquet (22 MB vs 2.4 MB, same data).
data/processed/master.csv

# --- Gradient-boosted model-selection artefacts (578 MB). These are the
# --- NEGATIVE results of Section 4.4; their accuracy numbers are reported in
# --- reports/ and the paper, and they are regenerable from
# --- scripts/train_models_v2.py / train_v3.py / train_v4.py. The released
# --- model, models/nn/, IS tracked.
models/*.txt
models/*.json
models/*.joblib
models/*.pt
models/v2/
models/v3/
models/v4/

# --- Local build artefacts
paper/_review.html
paper/.manuscript.tex.bak
paper/manuscript_review.pdf
reports/functional_form_search_prev.csv

# --- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
